      "id": "f1-evidence-fit",
      "class": "follow-up",
      "origin": "new",
      "at": "payload/.joycraft/references/testing-page.md:27",
      "summary": "Against sota-playbook.md section 1, the nine are not the nine best-evidenced. Principles 1, 2 and 9 all restate P8 (tiers), so three slots carry one principle. Principle 8 \"extend before adding\" has no ranked principle behind it (only checklist row 12). Missing S-graded principles: P7 flaky means defective, never retry into a pass, repeat a new or changed test file before it counts (the map row says \"slow or flaky\", yet the page has no flaky rule: probe NOTE); P1 no special-casing of test inputs and never edit the check that judges the change (the sota-evidence panel calls it the cheapest measured mitigation); P4 prove a new test can fail on a broken copy. Suggest folding 2 and 9 into 1 and using the freed slots for P7 and P1.",
      "assumption": "The spec fixes the nine items by name, so the page matches the spec; this is a spec-level change for the owner, not a failure of spec-20-1."
    },
    {
      "id": "f2-useful-tool",
